+# The integral comparison is complete; universal source occupancy is not
+
+Keep this at Turn 7. No original state at arbitrary hard p has been forced.
+The attached degree-eight construction has now been specialized at every actual
+original E/M source in its p=1 mod12 domain. Its original integral defects are
+computed, not erased by rank or norm equivalence.
+
+Completed statements:
+- Literal E completion has normalization index p^2, M has p^9, with exact
+  conductor ideals, invariant factors and original T/eta actions.
+- Generic literal rational-point counts are E0/4 and M4/8; all four occur at1009.
+  Do not apply the older reciprocal-cubic three-point count here.
+- The added E point lifts modp^2 (p choices) but not modp^3. Proper finite flatness
+  preserves length, not that integral section. Its physical xi pole is retained.
+- Prime-only sign and denominator-only sign need nonintegral original projector
+  coefficients; normalization restores those symmetries with its actual index.
+- Literal E/M rational comparison is integral one way and has exact p^2 loss the
+  other. An actual antecedent capacity crossing supplies the target in the example.
+- For any fixed finite set of places, one foreign prime yields joint numerical
+  E/M candidates satisfying the full numerical range, both gates, p-local
+  completion data and supplied real bounds, but violating u|a^2 in one occurrence.
+  This is a counterexample to that certificate predicate, not to ES or all-local
+  integrality. The same primes have genuine independent E and M endpoint states.
+
+Implication not supplied:
+  for every hard prime p, find u in an ORIGINAL square-divisor box with an E/M gate.
+The preceding capacity classification proves why same-grade search can exhaust
+all words and still fail. A new source-changing arrow must preserve or rebuild
+that actual global exponent box. Finite local signatures, nilpotent length, a
+rational inverse and the stated real estimates cannot be substituted for it.
+
+Suggested proof target, without assuming it:
+Construct a mechanism on the complete first-half source that either produces an
+original opposite divisor pair or proves a uniform nonzero lower bound for its
+integer coefficient. Its validation must precede the geometric transport.
+
+Permanent controls:
+- p1009,a253,u11 is E with zero local literal signed points, but M with eight.
+- The E boundary at p13 lifts modp^2 and fails at the root equation modp^3.
+- M's length-six special block is not F_p[eta]/eta^6; eta blocks are4+2.
+- N/S is not a quotient ring. Original defect actions are not arbitrary matrices.
+- p35281,a8821,u202883 has a single forbidden occurrence23. Both numerical gates
+  pass and all given local/height controls pass, but the original box does not.
+- The correct printed M rational numerator at p35281 is2489709608. The code
+  includes an exact printed-example check; the E local point count is0 and M4.
+- The p825241 channel return is the earlier noncanonical cofactor word25. Its
+  existence is not a consequence of the interpolation which compares it.
+
+No whole-history audit, remote PR, new overall ES range or Lean build is asserted
+unless a separate actual execution/publication receipt explicitly says so.
